er":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Intensive Case Management, Recovery and Employment (ICARE)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":502.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":196.0,"r":596.0,"t":520.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,58],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"Intensive Case Management, Recovery and Employment (ICARE)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The ICARE program began as a pilot program in Albuquerque and is designed to address substance use barriers to employment in TANF Recipients . The ICARE program now provides services in Albuquerque and Rio Arriba County.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":453.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.0,"r":659.3333333333334,"t":490.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,220],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"The ICARE program began as a pilot program in Albuquerque and is designed to address substance use barriers to employment in TANF Recipients . The ICARE program now provides services in Albuquerque and Rio Arriba County."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"It is a new approach that combines 12 weeks of Intensive Case Management with job readiness classes and job development. TANF recipients identified as having substance use issues that prevent them from obtaining and retaining employment are referred to the ICARE program: The program includes motivational interviewing t0 motivate change and decrease substance use; relapse prevention to build skills; family management to improve family functioning; job readiness classes to enhance employment skills and increase retention; and job development to secure employment. A program evaluation component will be used to determine the effectiveness of this program in addressing substance use disorders among TANF recipients.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":330.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.33333333333333,"r":715.3333333333334,"t":449.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,719],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"It is a new approach that combines 12 weeks of Intensive Case Management with job readiness classes and job development. TANF recipients identified as having substance use issues that prevent them from obtaining and retaining employment are referred to the ICARE program: The program includes motivational interviewing t0 motivate change and decrease substance use; relapse prevention to build skills; family management to improve family functioning; job readiness classes to enhance employment skills and increase retention; and job development to secure employment. A program evaluation component will be used to determine the effectiveness of this program in addressing substance use disorders among TANF recipients."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"10","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":50.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":390.6666666666667,"r":402.6666666666667,"t":60.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"10"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"NMWorks","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":25.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":659.3333333333334,"r":719.3333333333334,"t":42.0},"charspan":[0,7],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"NMWorks"}],"version":"1.10.0"}